# Contact details for the rendered CV.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and read automatically by `make`. Nothing here is ever
# committed, and CI sets none of it - so the HTML published to GitHub Pages
# carries no home address and no phone number, which is deliberate. A build
# with these unset succeeds and simply omits the lines.
#
# The values below are placeholders. This file is committed to a public repo,
# so the real ones only ever go in .env. Quotes are optional, and anything
# already exported in your shell takes precedence over this file.
#
# The email address is not here - it is publishable, and hardcoded in the
# Makefile.

# Home address, as one line, exactly as it should appear on the CV.
CV_ADDRESS="1 Example Street, Placeholder Town, AB1 2CD"

# Phone number, formatted as it should appear.
CV_PHONE="07000000000"
